Package: emlR
Title: All Elementary Functions from a Single Binary Operator
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Philipp", "Thoss", , "ph.thoss@gmx.de", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4672-2792"))
Description: An R implementation of the EML (Exp-Minus-Log) Sheffer
    operator from Odrzywolek (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2603.21852>,
    which proves that a single binary operator eml(x, y) = exp(x) -
    log(y), together with the constant 1, generates all elementary
    functions. The package provides the operator, native R-AST
    identity catalog, peephole simplifier with two modes
    (stays-in-EML and collapses-to-base-R), a stack-machine bytecode
    compiler for vectorised evaluation, and a depth-n master formula
    with L-BFGS-B fitter for symbolic regression.
